WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.131
Synthetic media includes generated or altered images, video, audio, text, documents,

00:00:05.131 --> 00:00:06.046
and screenshots.

00:00:06.046 --> 00:00:11.534
Deepfakes can represent people, events, actions, or statements, but not every edit,

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:15.193
suspicious artifact, or false caption is a deepfake.

00:00:15.193 --> 00:00:19.309
Misleading media can be fully synthetic, partly manipulated, staged,

00:00:19.309 --> 00:00:21.138
or genuine but miscontextualized.

00:00:21.138 --> 00:00:24.797
Visual and audio warning signs help form questions,

00:00:24.797 --> 00:00:28.914
yet compression and ordinary processing can create similar artifacts.

00:00:28.914 --> 00:00:32.115
Absence of artifacts does not prove authenticity.

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:36.231
Verification combines provenance, source history, reverse image comparison, keyframes,

00:00:36.231 --> 00:00:40.348
metadata, timelines, location or time clues, and independent corroboration.

00:00:40.348 --> 00:00:45.836
Detection tools remain one fallible input with false positives, false negatives, drift,

00:00:45.836 --> 00:00:47.208
and platform effects.

00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:49.952
Responsible reporting distinguishes unverified, manipulated, synthetic,

00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:51.324
and miscontextualized content.

00:00:51.324 --> 00:00:53.611
It states evidence, confidence, limitations,

00:00:53.611 --> 00:00:57.727
and alternative explanations while protecting sensitive people and material.

00:00:57.727 --> 00:01:02.758
The goal is disciplined analysis rather than panic or instant certainty.

00:01:02.758 --> 00:01:05.502
Preserve context, test claims, communicate carefully,

00:01:05.502 --> 00:01:10.991
and use media verification to support accountable decisions without creating additional reputational,

00:01:10.991 --> 00:01:12.820
privacy, or safety harm.
